            "text": "API keys",
            "level": 1
          },
          {
            "kind": "styled",
            "id": "dk11",
            "text": "Keys authenticate every request. Keep secret keys on the server, and rotate them when in doubt.",
            "style": {
              "size": 16,
              "color": "#425466"
            }
          },
          {
            "kind": "text",
            "id": "dk12",
            "text": "Publishable keys (pk_live_ and pk_test_) are safe to embed in a browser or mobile app; they can only create tokens and confirm payments the server set up. Secret keys (sk_live_ and sk_test_) can do anything the account can do and must never leave your server or be committed to a repository."
          },
          {
            "kind": "text",
            "id": "dk13",
            "text": "Restricted keys (rk_) grant a chosen subset of permissions, for example read-only access to Charges for a reporting job. Create them in the Dashboard under Developers, then API keys. Rolling a key gives you a grace period of up to 24 hours before the old key stops working."
          },
